<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13142" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπό-λῠσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>loosing,</i> e.g. of a bandage or cord, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
				<u>Aut.</u>
				2.9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>release, deliverance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Cra.</u>
				405b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				33.1.5
			</span></i>: c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ τὴν ἀ. τοῦ
			θανὰτου</span> as far as <i>acquittal from</i> a capital
			charge went, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.136
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ.</span>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακῶν θάνατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Arat.</u>
					54
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πένθους</span>
			<i>end</i> of mourning, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				56.53
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Canopus</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>getting rid of a disease,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Coac.</u>
				378
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>spell for releasing</i> a divine being, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Par.</u>
				1.1056
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (from 
				Pass.
			) <i>separation, parting,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				718a14
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ψυχῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>R.</u>
					479a22
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>decease, death,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.16.8
			</span></i>, Lycon ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				5.71
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ποιεῖσθαι</span> to take
			one's <i>departure,</i> of an army, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.69.10
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
